        "id": "ch1_8-1",
        "text": "Python development environments\nText editors are a tempting choice for editing Python code. But for any medium-to-\nlarge-sized project, we have to seriously consider Python integrated development\nenvironments ( IDEs ), which are very helpful for writing, debugging, and troubleshooting\nthe code using the version control and facilitating ease of deployments. There are many\nIDEs available, mostly free, on the market. In this section, we will review a few of them.\nNote that we will not try to rank them in any order but will emphasize the value each\nof them brings, and it is up to the reader to make the best choice based on their past\nexperience, project requirements, and the complexity of their projects.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 IDLE\n\u2022 Sublime Text\n\u2022 PyCharm\n\u2022 Visual Studio Code\n\u2022 PyDev\n\u2022 Spyder\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
